    "question_id": "math-2f9d66f560e25450",
    "question": "15. 8__(7___ 3)___ 9=20\n\nIntroduction to Expressions )\n\nIn Maths letters are sometimes used to stand for numbers. It is quicker to write a\nletter, such as 'n', than to write out the words 'a number'. Here the letter 'n'\nstands for a number, the value of which is not yet known.\n\nn+ 1 isa short way of saying that 1 is added to that number.\n\nn x 4 means the number is multiplied by 4.\n\nAny letter of the alphabet can be used to stand for a number.\n\nHowever, when using letters in Maths, be careful to write them clearly.\n\nIt is easy to confuse the letter b with the number 6, z for 2 and s for 5 unless\nyour handwriting is clear.\n\nPage 2 of 10",
    "questiontopic": "Unclassified",
    "answer": "",
    "explanation": ""
  },
  {
