  {
    "question_id": "math-f3b418d03a343acb",
    "question": "8. 7 lots off=\n\nBrackets are often used to group things together. The expression y + 6 can also\nbe written as (y + 6).\n\nIf the expression is multiplied by 3 it can be written as (y + 6) x 3 or 3 x (y + 6)\nbut is more simply written as 3(y + 6).\n\n3(y + 6) means 8 lots of (y + 6).\n\nWrite these more simply:",
    "questiontopic": "Unclassified",
    "answer": "",
    "explanation": ""
